{# =========================================================================
   Herald CP shared layout.

   Parent template for every screen in the Herald CP section (Settings,
   Temporary grants, Tokens, Activity, Connection). Extends `_layouts/cp`
   directly per locked decision 1 + cp.md §"Tabbed Settings Pages" — the
   plugin owns the full template lineage.

   The Gate 9 CP rework replaced the in-page tab bar with Craft's standard
   global-sidebar subnav (`Herald::getCpNavItem()`). Subtemplates set
   `selectedSubnavItem` to the subnav key Craft should highlight — one of
   `settings`, `grants`, `tokens`, `activity`, `connection` — and override
   `{% block content %}` with their body. The subnav itself is rendered by
   Craft from the section nav item; this template no longer paints tabs.

   Per locked decision 6 the only plugin-side asset bundle Gate 9 ships is
   `HeraldCpAsset` — registered here so every screen inherits it without
   per-template duplication.
   ========================================================================= #}

{% extends "_layouts/cp" %}

{% do view.registerAssetBundle("craftpulse\\herald\\web\\assets\\cp\\HeraldCpAsset") %}

{% set title = 'Herald'|t('herald') %}
{% set selectedSubnavItem = selectedSubnavItem ?? 'settings' %}
{% set docTitle = (selectedSubnavItem)|capitalize ~ ' - Herald' %}

{% block content %}
    {# Default content block — every concrete screen overrides this. #}
{% endblock %}
